\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Local paired-link source. (a) One bulk corner is attached to both line endpoints by physical diagonal springs. The $X/R$ variables are exact linear combinations of their signed harmonic extensions. (b) For positive segment extension, the line-driven radial component points toward the line at all four corner sites $(s_y a/2,s_z a/2)$. The arrows show only $\bm  {F}^{\rm  src}_{R,ic}$; the complete corner force also contains the axial source and displacement-dependent restoring terms. The exact resultant, torque, and first moment are given in Eqs.~\eqref  {eq:s3-radial-balance}--\eqref  {eq:s3-radial-dipole}.}}{6}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:s3-mechanism}{{2}{6}{Local paired-link source. (a) One bulk corner is attached to both line endpoints by physical diagonal springs. The $X/R$ variables are exact linear combinations of their signed harmonic extensions. (b) For positive segment extension, the line-driven radial component points toward the line at all four corner sites $(s_y a/2,s_z a/2)$. The arrows show only $\vF ^{\rm src}_{R,ic}$; the complete corner force also contains the axial source and displacement-dependent restoring terms. The exact resultant, torque, and first moment are given in Eqs.~\eqref {eq:s3-radial-balance}--\eqref {eq:s3-radial-dipole}}{figure.2}{}}
